Howdy,

I was checking out the Wizard mode, just to see what all I had been 
missing, and something particularly ODD happened...

I had the Amulet of Yendor.  I was all the way back to level 1.  Guess who 
shows up... Well, he stole the amulet.  Fearing that I might have to trek 
all the way back down to his level, I wished for a cursed Amulet of Yendor 
out of frustration.

I got one.

So I identified it.  I knew from experience what you usually got when you 
wished for this goody.

I got one.

Anyways, the Wizard shows up again and we have a grand ol' slugfest.  I 
kill him.  And guess what:  I got a SECOND Amulet of Yendor!  When I 
picked it up, I got a message about something probably being wrong, and 
hadn't I better quit.  I didn't.

As it turned out, I offered one of them on the altar of Law, and somebody 
ELSE accepted the offering!  Then a cloud of orange smoke appeared around 
me, and the game tallied up my points.  Odd.

Is this supposed to happen?

